{"name":"Golden Apples","hex":"#f3d74f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden apples","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of golden apple"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden_apples"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden apple","blocks":[{"text":"The golden apple is an element that appears in various legends that depict a hero retrieving the golden apples hidden or stolen by an antagonist. Gold apples also appear on the Silver Branch of the Otherworld in Irish mythology."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_apple","wikidata":"Q20894779"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Guido_Reni_-_Atalanta_and_Hippomenes_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/500px-Guido_Reni_-_Atalanta_and_Hippomenes_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam